> chaotic altar, so is Magicbane worth wish ? Boots of speed ? Gauntlets
> of dexterity ?  but if I'd wear gauntlets of dexterity I'll have to
> remove gauntlets of power, which are very helpful. Helm of brilliance
> (unwise have only 16 Int) ? Should I keep couple of wishes in reserve
> or because I'm newbie I better spend all at once ?

Magicbane isn't worth the wish, you'll get it as your first sac gift.
Do you have a reliable means of Elbereth for emergencies (wand of
fire/lightning/digging)?

I'd go for jumping boots over speed _if_ you'll remember  to use them.

Helm of brilliance is only worth it if you're orcish, IMO.  Gauntlets
of dex are fairly worthless, especially after you max your luck.

Magic marker (to boost AC) is a good idea.  The blessed Master Key of
Thievery will give you 1/2 physical damage, which is quite nice, and
teleport control, which is awesome (but as a wizard you'll get it
eventually--having it in the interim is valuable though).

I'd probably go with more than one marker, depending on the armor
situation and my needs.  I'd be quite tempted to use one to write
?genocide and eliminate L and h.

=conflict, or a /poly to polypile for it, are possibilities--conflict
can get you out of a lot of tight spots.

I'd keep only the last wrest charge in reserve in case you need an
unforeseen item before the Castle.

Whatever you decide on, your primary goal is to get things that will
help you survive to the Castle, where you'll get _another_ /wishing to
fill out any holes in your kit.



